        "original_id": "a2d5930c-f69b-526f-9842-79c404058417",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Laws: NICS Improvement Amendments Act of 2007\n- Systems: National Instant Criminal Background Check System (NICS)\n- People: Seung-Hui Cho\n- Events: Virginia Tech shootings\n- Places: Virginia Polytechnic Institute and State University, Blacksburg, Virginia\n\nFacts:\n- Seung-Hui Cho was born on January 18, 1984, and died on April 16, 2007.\n- On April 16, 2007, Seung-Hui Cho killed 32 people and wounded 17 others with two semi-automatic pistols at the Virginia Polytechnic Institute and State University in Blacksburg, Virginia.\n- Before the Virginia Tech shootings, a Virginia court had ruled that Seung-Hui Cho was a danger to himself.\n- In 2007, the NICS Improvement Amendments Act was passed in the wake of the Virginia Tech shootings.\n- The NICS Improvement Amendments Act of 2007 was intended to address loopholes in the National Instant Criminal Background Check System, commonly known as NICS.\n- Loopholes in the National Instant Criminal Background Check System enabled Seung-Hui Cho to buy firearms despite the Virginia court ruling.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
